  "explanation": "<h3>Basis before liability increase and distribution</h3><p>$40,000 + $10,000 + $12,000 = $62,000.</p><h3>Basis immediately before distribution</h3><p>Add the $8,000 liability-share increase.</p><h3>Gain on the cash distribution</h3><p>$75,000 cash exceeds $70,000 outside basis by $5,000.</p><h3>Remaining outside basis</h3><p>The distribution reduces basis to zero; the excess is gain rather than negative basis.</p>"
